.TH basename 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
basename \- strip directory and suffix from a name
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B basename
.I name
[\fIsuffix\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B basename
removes any trailing slashes from
.IR name ,
then everything up to and including the last remaining slash, and
prints what is left.  If
.I suffix
is given and
.I name
ends with it, that is removed too.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# basename /usr/man/man1/ls.1
ls.1
# basename /usr/man/man1/ls.1 .1
ls
.fi
.SH NOTES
With no arguments, or with more than two,
.B basename
prints nothing and exits 0.
.PP
A suffix is not removed if doing so would leave nothing, so
.B basename .1 .1
prints
.BR .1 .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dirname (1)
